{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The burden of Damascus. Instructed.</b> From the root of סיר (Isaiah 18:5)." "<b>From being.</b> From being a city. And if it is masculine language, the correct interpretation is that it concerns the people of Damascus, and the witness is והיתה." "<b>ערים מושים.</b> Like ערים נצורים (2 Kings 17:9), and it is as if it says מעי, like לעיים (Psalms 79:1), and the mem is added."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:04.746526486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}